218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 46 0 R
/T (Globally, CY 2025 was a strong year for equities. The MSCI ACWI rose 22%, while emerging markets outperformed developed markets, with the MSCI EM gaining 34% in dollar terms. China and Brazil stood out, with the MSCI China up 31% and MSCI Brazil rallying nearly 50%. In contrast, MSCI India delivered a modest 3% return in dollar terms, reflecting currency depreciation and relative underperformance. Among developed markets, Japan, the UK, Germany, and France posted strong double-digit gains. The S&P 500 rose 16%, while the tech-heavy NASDAQ 100 surged 24%, led by continued enthusiasm around Artificial Intelligence.)
/E (Globally, CY 2025 was a strong year for equities. The MSCI ACWI rose 22%, while emerging markets outperformed developed markets, with the MSCI EM gaining 34% in dollar terms. China and Brazil stood out, with the MSCI China up 31% and MSCI Brazil rallying nearly 50%. In contrast, MSCI India delivered a modest 3% return in dollar terms, reflecting currency depreciation and relative underperformance. Among developed markets, Japan, the UK, Germany, and France posted strong double-digit gains. The S&P 500 rose 16%, while the tech-heavy NASDAQ 100 surged 24%, led by continued enthusiasm around Artificial Intelligence.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
