/S /H2
/P 46 0 R
/T (On the monetary front, the RBI cut repo rates by a cumulative 125 basis points during the year. Long-term bond yields declined in the first half of 2025 and have since remained range-bound, with the 10-year G-Sec yield hovering around 6.6%. Short-term yields also traded in a narrow range, with the 364-day Treasury Bill yield near 2.6%. Inflation moderated meaningfully during the year, with WPI inflation turning negative in the final two months. While global rate cuts and easing inflation could allow the RBI to lower rates further in 2026, it will need to carefully balance currency stability and growth objectives.)
/E (On the monetary front, the RBI cut repo rates by a cumulative 125 basis points during the year. Long-term bond yields declined in the first half of 2025 and have since remained range-bound, with the 10-year G-Sec yield hovering around 6.6%. Short-term yields also traded in a narrow range, with the 364-day Treasury Bill yield near 2.6%. Inflation moderated meaningfully during the year, with WPI inflation turning negative in the final two months. While global rate cuts and easing inflation could allow the RBI to lower rates further in 2026, it will need to carefully balance currency stability and growth objectives.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [11 12]
