endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Systematic Withdrawal Plan \(SWP\) is a mutual funds facility using which you can draw fixed amounts from your mutual fund investment at regular intervals \(e.g. monthly, any other interval as specified by the AMC\). SWP works by redeeming the required number of units at prevailing NAVs to meet your SWP cash-flows. The SWP will continue as long you have sufficient unit balance to meet your cash-flows. In this article we will compare SWP with IDCW option \(dividends\))
/E (Systematic Withdrawal Plan \(SWP\) is a mutual funds facility using which you can draw fixed amounts from your mutual fund investment at regular intervals \(e.g. monthly, any other interval as specified by the AMC\). SWP works by redeeming the required number of units at prevailing NAVs to meet your SWP cash-flows. The SWP will continue as long you have sufficient unit balance to meet your cash-flows. In this article we will compare SWP with IDCW option \(dividends\))
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 924 0 R
/T (Mutual fund dividends are paid out at the discretion of the fund manager and the asset management company \(AMC\). The fund may declare / increase the dividend payout rate or may even not pay dividends \(IDCW\) for a certain period depending on market conditions. )
/E (Mutual fund dividends are paid out at the discretion of the fund manager and the asset management company \(AMC\). The fund may declare / increase the dividend payout rate or may even not pay dividends \(IDCW\) for a certain period depending on market conditions. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 925 0 R
/T (In mutual fund systematic withdrawal plans \(SWP\), investors can get fixed cash-flows every month \(or any other frequencies\), as per their own specific needs. Unlike dividends, SWP provides fixed cash-flows to the investor till there is enough balance units to generate the SWP cash shows. )
/E (In mutual fund systematic withdrawal plans \(SWP\), investors can get fixed cash-flows every month \(or any other frequencies\), as per their own specific needs. Unlike dividends, SWP provides fixed cash-flows to the investor till there is enough balance units to generate the SWP cash shows. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 926 0 R
/T (SWP gives investors more control over their finances. In IDCW option profits made by the fund are distributed to the investor as IDCW payment or dividend. In SWP, you can withdraw according to your needs. If your SWP withdrawal is less than profit, then the profits remain invested in the scheme and gives you compounding benefits. You can get both fixed cash-flows and capital appreciation in SWP. )
/E (SWP gives investors more control over their finances. In IDCW option profits made by the fund are distributed to the investor as IDCW payment or dividend. In SWP, you can withdraw according to your needs. If your SWP withdrawal is less than profit, then the profits remain invested in the scheme and gives you compounding benefits. You can get both fixed cash-flows and capital appreciation in SWP. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 927 0 R
/T (However, if your withdrawal rate is high then you may end up with no balance units before the tenure of your SWP. Under SEBI regulations mutual fund dividends are paid only from the accumulated profits of the scheme. In prolonged bear markets, a scheme may stop paying dividends \(IDCW\). On the other hand, in SWP, you will have to redeem more units for the same SWP withdrawal every month when NAVs are falling. )
/E (However, if your withdrawal rate is high then you may end up with no balance units before the tenure of your SWP. Under SEBI regulations mutual fund dividends are paid only from the accumulated profits of the scheme. In prolonged bear markets, a scheme may stop paying dividends \(IDCW\). On the other hand, in SWP, you will have to redeem more units for the same SWP withdrawal every month when NAVs are falling. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 928 0 R
/T (SWP is much more tax efficient compared to IDCW in equity funds or equity oriented. Withdrawals from equity funds made a year after investment is subject to long term capital gains taxation. Long-term capital gains up to Rs 1.5 lakh every year are tax free and taxed at 12.5% thereafter. Dividends paid by mutual funds are taxed in the hands of the investor at the tax slab rate of the investor.)
/E (SWP is much more tax efficient compared to IDCW in equity funds or equity oriented. Withdrawals from equity funds made a year after investment is subject to long term capital gains taxation. Long-term capital gains up to Rs 1.5 lakh every year are tax free and taxed at 12.5% thereafter. Dividends paid by mutual funds are taxed in the hands of the investor at the tax slab rate of the investor.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
